 (verdict Reject)
 (notes
  "GRID DOES NOT CLEAR - 12%-weekly is NOT promotable; it keeps its single-surface ACCEPT and stays a default-off axis (experiment-flag-discipline R3 not satisfied). Every 5y pair loses on BOTH criteria (3 of 3 salts on both cells): 2019 s0 realised $469k -> $166k, maxDD 22.6 -> 30.9; 2019 s1 $258k -> $207k, 22.5 -> 31.1; 2019 s2 $245k -> $213k, 22.8 -> 31.2; 2009 s0 $106k -> -$23k (-$139k ex-twin), 17.9 -> 27.1; 2009 s1 $277k -> $10k (-$277k ex-twin), 20.4 -> 25.2; 2009 s2 $77k -> -$12k (-$99k ex-twin), 17.1 -> 25.4 (the +12pp level is $268k open MTM). Sharpe worse in five of six. The consistent per-year loser is 2021 on the 2019 cell (-$280k / -$261k / -$265k vs +$72k / -$61k / -$65k) and 2010 on the 2009 cell: in a chop year the 12% stop turns a 4% whipsaw into a 12% bleed (loser sums 1.4-1.7x) and nothing runs far enough to pay for it; the 26y cell shows the same 2021 loss at every salt, swamped there by 2020 and 2023 - whose biggest wide winners (CLS, BFX, TTEC, CLFD, $2.6M) are absent from the 2019 composition, which shares only 1,023 of ~2,980 names with the 2000 composition. WHY (transferable): the mechanism's one salt-robust term - the SHARED trades run wider - is positive in every cell (+$0.6-2.0M at 26y; +$271k/+$250k on 2019; +$84k/+$104k on 2009). The sign flips on the 5y cells through the path re-draw (arm-only minus null-only -$0.57M/-$0.30M on 2019, -$0.21M/-$0.37M on 2009 vs +$2.0M/~0/+$0.8M at 26y) and through the drawdown episode: from equity_curve.csv the null's 2019 maxDD is the Covid crash (2020-02-12 -> 03-23) while the wide arm's is the 2021-05-07 -> 2023-10-27 grind, and on 2009 the arm's episode starts at the 2010 flash-crash and runs to 2012-06 while the null's is the shorter 2011-12 leg. A 12% stop re-evaluated weekly holds slow losers longer and carries more open names through a grind (11 vs 7 at the 2019 end). WIDE-WEEKLY IS REGIME-DEPENDENT: it wins where the drawdown is a fast crash followed by a recovery (the 26y tape; same shape as project_stop_width_regime_dependent for 5.9% on 2000-04) and loses in slow grinds; the 26y ACCEPT is a composition in which the recovery term dominates. Same lesson as the 2026-05-30 early-admission grid: the long-window winner did not generalise to an independent context. Force liquidations on the wide cells were dissected (README): all Per_position breaker fires labelled stop_loss, 6 of 7 real earnings gaps, 1 phantom (SGP_old1 stub prints on a series that should end at the 2009-11 Merck merger, -$60k/salt) - not a blocker and not the reason. CONSEQUENCES: no promotion PR; the 10%-weekly neighbour arm is not owed (same plateau, reversal is directional); cancel-resting-longs-on-Bearish (item 3) loses its motivation because that cohort is POSITIVE on the record convention (+$0.12/+$0.22/+$0.19M) and only negative on the wide arm - no build for now, brief kept. Exit stack on the record stays SETTLED; the gap is entry-side (project_exit_stack_survives_fixed_basis). Artifacts: cadence-12w-v10-2026-09-13/results/{n5,a4}-{2009,2019}-s{0,1,2}-v10-* (actual, trades, params, summary, open_positions, force_liquidations, validator). Related: 2026-09-13-stop-width-12pct-weekly-cadence-v10dedup (the single-surface ACCEPT), 2026-09-09-stop-width-by-macro-state-surface, 2026-05-30 early-admission grid (dev/notes/early-admission-surface-v2-2026-05-30.md)."))
